{
    "source": {
        "directories": ["src"]
    },
    // The full suite takes ~30s on a developer machine, well past Infection's 10s default. With that
    // default, every mutant whose covering tests reach the integration suite came back as "required
    // more time than configured", which Infection counts as *detected*: 253 of 269 mutants timed out,
    // 16 were actually killed, and the gate still reported MSI 100% and exited 0, i.e. it could not
    // fail. A timeout has to exceed the slowest covering test run, not the fastest. With 180 the
    // only mutants that time out are the two genuine infinite loops in
    // RepositoryMetadataLoader::loadChunked() (the `!== []` loop guard and the splice offset), which
    // Infection counts as detected — correctly, since a test that never returns is a failing test.
    "timeout": 180,
    "logs": {
        "text": "build/infection.log"
    },
    "mutators": {
        "@default": true
    },
    // Scope widened to src/Output + src/Analyzer on 2026-09-16. Before: 1175 mutants, 76 escaped,
    // MSI 93.53%; 67 of those were closed, most by tests and the rest by removing the code they sat
    // in, and 4 more turned out to be equivalent (see the tests and refactors of that date). After: 1130 mutants, 9 escaped, 0 timed out -> MSI = Covered MSI 99.2%, ~1m35s on
    // 8 threads. Each escape was checked by hand and is equivalent, the honest floor of this scope
    // (the reasoning, with every later escape, is in tests/infection-equivalents.md):
    //  - src/Signal/ConstraintOpenness.php (5: CastInt x2, IncrementInteger, DecrementInteger,
    //    ConcatOperandRemoval): numeric strings compare numerically, every mutated integer stays
    //    below any PHP major, and normalize("8.4") equals normalize("8.4.0").
    //  - src/Analyzer/Report.php flagged() UnwrapArrayValues: the findings are sorted and every
    //    flagged one precedes every unflagged one, so the filtered keys are already 0..n; the
    //    array_values() is what makes the `list` type true by construction.
    //  - src/Output/JsonFormatter.php format() FalseValue: the `$showAll` default of the interface's
    //    parameter, which the JSON document does not read (it always lists every finding).
    //  - src/Output/TableFormatter.php label() CastString: previousVerdictOf() is never null once
    //    the comparison says "worsened"; the cast is for the type, not for a case.
    //  - src/Output/TerminalWidth.php detect() Coalesce: step 2 (symfony Terminal) refuses whenever
    //    COLUMNS is set, so swapping it with step 1 (COLUMNS) is unobservable by design.
    //
    // Re-measured 2026-09-16 with FailOn, the per-forge analyzer notes and the activity cache age
    // in scope: 1175 mutants, the same 9 escapes, MSI = Covered MSI 99.23%, ~1m40s on 8 threads.
    //
    // Widened to the whole src tree on 2026-09-17. Before: 3160 mutants, 269 escaped, MSI 91%.
    // 209 were closed by sharper tests, 9 by removing statements no test could observe (a redundant
    // array_unique, a sort over an already-sorted list, a root filter every walk guards against, a
    // trim its only reader repeats, an unused constructor parameter, Composer\Cache guards that
    // Cache::read()/write() already apply), and 47 more turned out to be equivalent. After: 3202
    // mutants (one added by the clock seam of that day), 56 escaped, 2 timed out (both genuine
    // infinite loops in RepositoryMetadataLoader::loadChunked(), i.e. detections), MSI = Covered MSI
    // 98.25%, ~6m20s on 8 threads locally. tests/infection-equivalents.md holds the reasoning for
    // all 56; the 47 added that day, one line each, as an index (line numbers moved on 2026-09-25
    // past the `@internal` docblock lines added that day, as in tests/infection-equivalents.md):
    //  - Set membership written as `= true` and read only through isset(): ActivityClient.php:82,
    //    ActivityFetchPlanner.php:53 and :69, RepositoryMetadataLoader.php:275 (TrueValue).
    //  - array_values() that only makes a `list` type true, every consumer iterates: ActivityClient.php:122,
    //    RepositoryMetadataLoader.php:73, InstallTimeSummary.php:118, LockrotCommand.php:368.
    //  - Casts the type system already guarantees: RepoLocator.php:141 and SupportSource.php:30
    //    (preg_replace with a literal pattern), PhpReleaseDates.php:30 (a `\d+.\d+` key is never an int),
    //    ComposerHttpClient.php:119 (substr of a host longer than 4) and :175 (`?? 0` on a ?int),
    //    LockrotCommand.php:108 and :165 (getcwd() false only in a removed working directory).
    //  - Memoisation of a pure function: AllowlistEntry.php:37 (VersionParser is stateless),
    //    BaselineSchema.php:72, ConfigSchema.php:56, DependencyGraph.php:116 (recomputed, equal answer).
    //  - Branches the shipped inputs cannot enter: BaselineSchema.php:43 x2 and ConfigSchema.php:44 x2
    //    (the PHPStan narrowing over json-schema errors, which are always arrays of strings),
    //    BaselineSchema.php:76 and ConfigSchema.php:60 (a schema shipped in the package is never
    //    unreadable), BaselineFile.php:114 (error_clear_last before a write that records its own
    //    warning) and :156 (error_get_last() is never null on that path), ProjectIgnoreList.php:72
    //    ((int) of the whole YYYY-MM-DD match is the year), HttpResult.php:85 (getLastErrors() is false
    //    on PHP >= 8.2 when clean; killed on the 7.4 leg), LockrotCommand.php:379 x2 (the Composer 2.2
    //    arm of the tryComposer() guard, never entered on the vendored Composer; covered by the Docker
    //    7.4/2.2 run outside Infection), SelfUpdateCommand.php:132 (Phar::running(false) differs only
    //    inside a running PHAR; covered by the e2e PharTest Infection does not run).
    //  - Same result by another route: ActivityClient.php:70 (`<` to `<=` assigns an equal value),
    //    ProjectIgnoreList.php:76 and PhpReleaseDates.php:30 Concat (PHP's date parser accepts the
    //    reversed `T..` concatenation as the same instant), JsonReader.php:86 (array_keys([]) never
    //    equals range(0, -1)), RepositoryMetadataLoader.php:159 and :201 (pass 2 after an exhausted
    //    deadline starts no chunk and marks the same names), ActivityFetchPlanner.php:62 x2 (the `?? 0`
    //    default inside the already-seen branch is unreachable), LockrotCommand.php:162 (the next
    //    statement raises the identical ConfigException), :374 (tryComposer() on a missing manifest
    //    returns null anyway), Policy.php:24 (FailOn::reaches() is false for `none`, the loop rejects
    //    everything and falls through to EXIT_OK), InstallTimeSummary.php:188 x2 (the stale list the
    //    names feed is never rendered on the install-time path; kept for a truthful comparison),
    //    SelfUpdateCommand.php:170 and :174 (an unclosed `</error>` renders byte-identically, the line
    //    is the command's last write).
    //  - 2026-09-18 (left-behind, advisories): ReleaseBranch.php:35 PregMatchRemoveCaret (a normalized
    //    non-dev version always starts with its major digits), LeftBehindRule.php:68
    //    LessThanOrEqualTo (a same-instant higher release cannot be both alive and older than the
    //    warn threshold), RepositoryAdvisoryLoader.php:69 ReturnRemoval (the Composer 2.2 arm, covered
    //    by the Docker 7.4/2.2 run).
    //
    // 2026-09-20 (JSON schemas, monorepo-dated branches): four new equivalents, all in
    // tests/infection-equivalents.md — Analyzer::dateSplitPackages() and
    // MonorepoParents::missingCandidates() early-return guards whose bodies are reached anyway,
    // the `= true` set membership in PackageMetadata::fromPackages() and the branch-snapshot guard
    // in needsParentDates(). Both CI shards re-measured against their own thresholds on the branch:
    // verdicts and output 99% covered MSI (11 escapes), data and the rest 98% (33 escapes).
    //
    // Threshold 97 = floor of the honest MSI minus 1: at 3201 mutants that leaves room for ~40 new
    // escapes before the gate fails — close to the ~25 the narrower scope allowed — without the
    // number moving every time a test is added.
    "minMsi": 97,
    "minCoveredMsi": 97
}
